WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.840
TRACE retrieves objects from clutter under arm occlusion.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.840
Withdrawing the arm restores visibility, but interrupts manipulation.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.840
The teacher plans once in simulation.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.840
The plan-conditioned student uses memory and partial feedback.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.840
Pushing continues without sensing retractions.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.840
TRACE achieves ninety percent success in hardware trials.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.840
Pushing needs no online search or simulation.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.840
The plan stays fixed; actions adapt as objects move.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.840
Demonstrations.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.573
Teacher Replay executes a fixed plan without object feedback.

00:00:33.573 --> 00:00:37.634
It cannot correct contact-induced deviations and may leave the target ungraspable.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:40.588
The online teacher achieves the highest hardware success,

00:00:40.588 --> 00:00:44.279
but repeatedly retracts the arm to recover complete scene state.

00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:47.971
P M B S, the previous state of the art,

00:00:47.971 --> 00:00:53.509
combines tree search with batched simulation; planning and scene reacquisition increase end to end time.

00:00:53.509 --> 00:00:55.725
Spiral is a target-centric pushing heuristic.

00:00:55.725 --> 00:01:00.155
It requires an updated target pose at each decision and retracts the

00:01:00.155 --> 00:01:02.370
arm when the target is occluded.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:06.431
Spiral is fastest on average, but unreliable in these tight workspaces,

00:01:06.431 --> 00:01:11.600
with lower success than TRACE and a substantial rate of out of workspace failures.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:17.873
TRACE uses one privileged rollout to guide feedback control under self occlusion.

00:01:17.873 --> 00:01:21.622
A complete initial observation initializes the digital twin,

00:01:21.622 --> 00:01:26.307
and the teacher produces a nominal plan before manipulation begins.

00:01:26.307 --> 00:01:30.525
During pushing, the recurrent student combines partial object observations,

00:01:30.525 --> 00:01:36.148
robot proprioception, memory, and local rollout context to select its next action.

00:01:36.148 --> 00:01:42.708
The nominal plan stays fixed, while the executed actions adapt to the observed scene.

00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:46.925
As contact moves objects away from their predicted positions,

00:01:46.925 --> 00:01:50.205
the controller can depart from the plan.

00:01:50.205 --> 00:01:56.297
The observation history records object visibility and the age of the last observation,

00:01:56.297 --> 00:02:00.045
retaining context when the arm blocks the view.

00:02:00.045 --> 00:02:06.137
No online teacher queries, simulator rollouts, or sensing retractions are required during pushing.

00:02:06.137 --> 00:02:09.417
The rollout defines the scene-specific execution horizon.

00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:14.103
The arm withdraws for the final graspability check before retrieval.

00:02:14.103 --> 00:02:19.726
This separates closed-loop pushing under partial visibility from the final check that

00:02:19.726 --> 00:02:21.600
requires a clear view.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:26.163
Across the hardware benchmark, TRACE achieves ninety percent success,

00:02:26.163 --> 00:02:30.511
with no observed workspace violations or sensing retractions during pushing.

00:02:30.511 --> 00:02:33.555
Its remaining failures reach the execution budget.

00:02:33.555 --> 00:02:37.034
TRACE is more reliable than replay and Spiral,

00:02:37.034 --> 00:02:42.251
and improves both success and total time over P M B S.

00:02:42.251 --> 00:02:44.425
Spiral remains faster on average.

00:02:44.425 --> 00:02:47.904
The online teacher reaches ninety five percent success;

00:02:47.904 --> 00:02:52.252
TRACE is two point nine times faster end to end.

00:02:52.252 --> 00:02:56.600
One initial plan supports adaptive execution without repeated complete-scene reacquisition.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.840
Plan conditioned retrieval.
